@startuml
title SD5 : Delivery record queried

actor "Compliance / Audit" as Audit
participant "//Communication Interaction Management//" as CIM
participant "Party Interaction Management" as PIM

Audit -> CIM : 1 **TMF681 Communication Management** GET /communicationMessage\n?receiver.party.id=Alice
activate CIM
CIM --> Audit : 2 **TMF681** 200 OK — four records for Alice\n(order confirmation "completed" · marketing offer "cancelled" ·\narrears notice "completed" · bill notice "completed")\neach with state, sendTime, sendTimeComplete, tryTimes, messageType
deactivate CIM

Audit -> PIM : 3 **TMF683 Party Interaction Management** GET /partyInteraction\n?relatedParty.id=Alice
activate PIM
PIM --> Audit : 4 **TMF683** 200 OK — four interactions\n(three outbound dispatched, and the inbound "STOP" of SD-2\ncarrying interactionRelationship to the notification it answered)
deactivate PIM

note across
  The query is answerable: what Alice was sent, when, on what
  channel, and that the marketing offer was suppressed while
  the arrears notice was not. Two properties are not
  represented in the published model: the reason a
  notification was not delivered, and the channel and
  address used where the route was substituted (§3.1.3).
end note

Audit -> CIM : 5 **TMF681** POST /hub\n(register a listener for delivery-state transitions)
activate CIM
CIM --> Audit : 6 **TMF681** 201 Created\n(the hub accepts the registration; v4.0.0 defines\nno event schema, so the payload is undefined)
deactivate CIM

note over CIM
  Delivery state is therefore available by query only (C4).
  TMF688 Event Management is deprecated, so there is no
  central event API to subscribe to instead: the events
  defined on TMF681 are the only event surface, and none
  are defined. Recorded in §5.1.3 and §5.1.7.
end note

@enduml
